From: arena agent (handoff)
Subject: [PATCH] Raise Ubuntu Rust-transcription CI timeout 20 -> 45 min

Apply with:  git apply docs/handoff/workflow-timeout.patch
(or `git am docs/handoff/workflow-timeout.patch` if you keep the mail headers)

This is the ONE change I could not push from the arena branch because the
GitHub App token for this session lacks the `workflows: write` permission.
Any branch that (via a stacked base) touches `.github/workflows/**` is
rejected with:

  refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow
  `.github/workflows/...` without `workflows` permission

Apply this on a device/token with `workflows` scope, then push.

--- a/.github/workflows/test-package-rust-transcription.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/test-package-rust-transcription.yml
@@ -17,7 +17,10 @@ jobs:
   test:
     name: Test Rust Transcription (${{ matrix.label }})
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
-    timeout-minutes: 20
+    # Ubuntu downloads ONNX/whisper model artifacts over the network during the
+    # ignored end-to-end integration tests; 20 minutes is too tight there (the
+    # macOS/Windows jobs finish in ~2-4 minutes). Raised so the slowest runner
+    # has headroom. A follow-up should cache the model artifacts instead of
+    # re-downloading them every run.
+    timeout-minutes: 45
     strategy:
       fail-fast: false
       matrix:
-- 
